<worksheet >
    <title>IC-2 Triple Integrals</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, you will need to correctly complete both problems. 
      To earn a P on this outcome, you will need to correctly complete Problem 1 and 
      one part of Problem 2</p>
  </introduction>  
  <page>
    <exercise workspace="2.5in">
      <p>Evaluate <m>\iiint_E 6xy dV</m> where 
        <m>E=\left\{(x,y,z)|0\le x\le3, 0\le y\le \sqrt{9-x^2}, 0\le z\le x\right\}</m></p>
</exercise>
  </page>
  <page>
    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
      <task><statement><p>Let <m>\iiint_D (x^2y+y^3) dV</m> be such that 
        <m>D</m> is the solid in the first octant that lies beneath the 
        paraboloid <m>z=4-x^2-y^2</m>. Use cylindrical coordinates to set 
        up the integration that will give the volume.</p></statement></task>
      <task><statement><p>Let <m>\iiint_D (x^2+y^2) dV</m> be such that 
        <m>D</m> is the region that lies between the spheres <m>\rho=1</m> 
        and <m>\rho=3</m>, and above the cone <m>\phi=\frac{\pi}{4}</m>. Use 
        spherical coordinates to set up the integration that will give the volume.</p></statement></task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>